From: Aryan Randeriya <aryan.k.randeriya@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 00:13:18 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 17/18] fix(stealth): a stealth page's scripts and form posts
 go out as the same browser as its pages

A stealth page loads documents, stylesheets, images and scripted fetches through
the wreq client, which presents the Linux Chrome 145 identity. Two requests
still went through the plain client and its profile identity (Windows Chrome
143, another TLS fingerprint):

- Parser-inserted classic scripts.
- Form submissions (POST navigations), and the redirect they answer with.

A site that pins its session to the User-Agent (Rack's session-hijacking guard,
as on the-internet.herokuapp.com) cleared the session on each script request,
and the cleared cookie replaced the signed-in one: a login made in the page
worked while the page was open, but the cookies saved from it were logged out.
Scripts now prefer the stealth client as stylesheets do, and the stealth client
gains post_form_with_callbacks: the same navigation loop with a method and a
body, a 301/302/303 answered with a GET, and no retry of a non-GET after a
connection reset.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tm2SNEJ42hMPiZ6cFb8Vih
